{"strongs": "H6776", "word": "צֶ֫מֶד", "translit": "tse.med", "root": "צמד", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "couple, pair", "definition": "צֶ֫מֶד noun masculine 1Kgs 19:19 couple, pair ; — ׳ צ construct Judg 19:3 +; suffix צִמְדּוֺ Jer 51:23 plural צְמָדִים 1Kgs 19:19 ; 2Kgs 9:25 (but see below); construct צִמְדֵּי Isa 5:10 ( Ges «GKC:93m»§ 93m ); — 1. couple, pair , usually of animals, חֲמֹרִים ׳ צ Judg 19:3 ; Judg 19:10 ; 2Sam 16:1 בָּקָר ( הַ ) ׳ צ span of oxen 1Sam 11:7 ; 1Kgs 19:21 , plural of more than one span v 1Kgs 19:19 (ploughing), Job 1:3 ; Job 42:12 צֶמֶד פְּרָדִים 2Kgs 5:17 פָּרָשִׁים ׳ צ Isa 21:7 ; Isa 21:9 a pair of horsemen ; plural also of one pair of riders 2Kgs 9:25 (but read probably צֶמֶד , so Kit ); ׳ צ alone = span (of oxen) Jer 51:23 . 2. a measure of land (only square measure in OT) like acre ; originally apparently what a span can plough (in a day; see Now Archaeology i. 202 Benz Archaeology 208 ; compare modern faddan , = what, can be ploughed in a season Schumacher ZPV xii (1889), 163 f. , Across Jordan 22, or in a day Bergheim PEQ, 1894, 192 , Ency. Bib. ACRE ), שָׂדֶה ׳ צ 1Sam 14:14 (on text see Dr HPS ); צִמְדֵּיכֶֿרֶם Isa 5:10 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB7108')\">BDB7108</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H6776')\">H6776</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB7107')\">BDB7107</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB7109')\">BDB7109</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>צֶ֫מֶד</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"1Kgs 19:19\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(11,19,19)\">1Kgs 19:19</ref></sup> <highlightword>couple, pair</highlightword>; — <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>צ</bdbheb> construct <ref ref=\"Judg 19:3\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(7,19,3)\">Judg 19:3</ref> +; suffix <bdbheb>צִמְדּוֺ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Jer 51:23\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"51\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"51\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(24,51,23)\">Jer 51:23</ref> plural <bdbheb>צְמָדִים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 19:19\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(11,19,19)\">1Kgs 19:19</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 9:25\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(12,9,25)\">2Kgs 9:25</ref> (but see below); construct <bdbheb>צִמְדֵּי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 5:10\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(23,5,10)\">Isa 5:10</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ges')\">Ges</lookup><sup>«GKC:93m»§ 93m</sup>); — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>couple, pair</highlight>, usually of animals, <bdbheb>חֲמֹרִים</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>צ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Judg 19:3\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(7,19,3)\">Judg 19:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Judg 19:10\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(7,19,10)\">Judg 19:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 16:1\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(10,16,1)\">2Sam 16:1</ref> <bdbheb>בָּקָר</bdbheb> (<bdbheb>הַ</bdbheb>) <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>צ</bdbheb> <highlight>span of oxen</highlight> <ref ref=\"1Sam 11:7\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(9,11,7)\">1Sam 11:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 19:21\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(11,19,21)\">1Kgs 19:21</ref>, plural of more than one span v<ref ref=\"1Kgs 19:19\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(11,19,19)\">1Kgs 19:19</ref> (ploughing), <ref ref=\"Job 1:3\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(18,1,3)\">Job 1:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Job 42:12\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"42\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"42\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(18,42,12)\">Job 42:12</ref> <bdbheb>צֶמֶד פְּרָדִים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Kgs 5:17\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(12,5,17)\">2Kgs 5:17</ref> <bdbheb>פָּרָשִׁים</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>צ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 21:7\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(23,21,7)\">Isa 21:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 21:9\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(23,21,9)\">Isa 21:9</ref> <highlight>a pair of horsemen</highlight>; plural also of one pair of riders <ref ref=\"2Kgs 9:25\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(12,9,25)\">2Kgs 9:25</ref> (but read probably <bdbheb>צֶמֶד</bdbheb>, so <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Kit')\">Kit</lookup>); <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>צ</bdbheb> alone = <highlight>span</highlight> (of oxen) <ref ref=\"Jer 51:23\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"51\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"51\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(24,51,23)\">Jer 51:23</ref>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> a measure of land (only square measure in OT) like <highlight>acre</highlight>; originally apparently what a <highlight>span</highlight> can plough (in a day; see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Now')\">Now<sup>Archaeology i. 202</sup></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Benz')\">Benz<sup>Archaeology 208</sup></lookup>; compare modern <highlight>faddan</highlight>, = what, can be ploughed in a season Schumacher<sup>ZPV xii (1889), 163 f.</sup>, Across Jordan 22, or in a day Bergheim<sup>PEQ, 1894, 192</sup>, Ency. Bib.<sup>ACRE</sup>), <bdbheb>שָׂדֶה</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>צ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Sam 14:14\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(9,14,14)\">1Sam 14:14</ref> (on text see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dr')\">Dr</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('HPS')\">HPS</lookup>); <bdbheb>צִמְדֵּיכֶֿרֶם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 5:10\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(23,5,10)\">Isa 5:10</ref>. </p></div><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "1Kgs 19:19", "book": "1KI", "chapter": 19, "verse": 19}, {"raw": "Judg 19:3",